From 22490744a2d7d368a7ad6ca32acb6b6b4a02161f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yury Klushin <digger@live.ru>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:40:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the pdp11-uknc SAV writer failing to replace its own
 output on Windows

The image is written beside the linked file and renamed over it, and
rename() on Windows will not write over a file that is already there:
"cannot rename hello.sav.sav-tmp to hello.sav: File exists".  Every
link of a .sav failed on a mingw-hosted toolchain, the very first one
being the hello example.

Removing the destination first is what rename() does for itself
everywhere else, and costs nothing there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11sav.em | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11sav.em b/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11sav.em
index 3240390b798..fbf8212cd09 100644
--- a/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11sav.em
+++ b/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11sav.em
@@ -139,6 +139,13 @@ gld${EMULATION_NAME}_after_close_output (void)
   if (!bfd_close (ibfd))
     fatal (_("%P: %s: final close failed: %E\n"), output_filename);
 
+  /* The linked file is still sitting there under the name the SAV image
+     is about to take, and on Windows rename() will not write over an
+     existing file the way it does everywhere else -- "cannot rename
+     hello.sav.sav-tmp to hello.sav: File exists".  Removing it first
+     costs nothing on a host where rename() would have done it.  */
+  unlink (output_filename);
+
   if (rename (tmp_filename, output_filename) != 0)
     fatal (_("%P: cannot rename %s to %s: %s\n"),
 	   tmp_filename, output_filename, strerror (errno));
